      "Name": "body",
      "Html": "\u003Cstyle class=\u0022code-analysis-syntax\u0022\u003E\n.docs-content pre{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0 1.75rem;padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;border:1px solid rgba(20,42,72,.16);border-left:4px solid #0e6fae;border-radius:4px;background:#f7fbfe;color:#10263a}\n.docs-content pre code{white-space:pre;color:inherit;background:transparent;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.65}\n.language-csharp .syntax-comment{color:#587287;font-style:italic}.language-csharp .syntax-string{color:#8a3d12}.language-csharp .syntax-keyword{color:#6542a6;font-weight:700}.language-csharp .syntax-number{color:#096b65}.language-csharp .syntax-type{color:#0a6680;font-weight:600}\n\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003EEvery public service method must be declared by its local interface.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat The Standard says\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026ldquo;public surface\u0026rdquo; \u0026mdash; The Standard deliberately limits what a component exposes. Requiring every public service operation to appear on its local interface prevents an undeclared concrete-class API from bypassing that contract. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard/blob/master/2.%20Services/2.%20Services.md#204-class-visibility-and-exposure-control\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003Eread it here\u003C/a\u003E.\u003Cbr\u003E\u0026ldquo;contract\u0026rdquo; \u0026mdash; The abstraction described for foundation services depends on upstream callers seeing a stable contract regardless of the underlying integration. The interface must therefore describe the complete public service surface. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard/blob/master/2.%20Services/2.1%20Foundations/2.1%20Foundations.md#2130-abstraction\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003Eread it here\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy it matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe local interface is only a truthful contract when it contains the complete public service surface. Extra public methods on the implementation create an unofficial API that bypasses abstraction, is harder to substitute, and can be consumed inconsistently.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EBad code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Violates STX0015: Every public service method must be declared by its local interface.\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Einterface\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentService\u003C/span\u003E { \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E\u0026lt;\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGetStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E studentId); }\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eclass\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudentService\u003C/span\u003E : \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentService\u003C/span\u003E\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Epublic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EDeleteStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E studentId) =\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Edefault\u003C/span\u003E;\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGood code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Follows STX0015\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Einterface\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIStudentService\u003C/span\u003E\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E\u0026lt;\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGetStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E studentId);\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EDeleteStudent\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EGuid\u003C/span\u003E studentId);\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E"
    }
